# Research Protocol

Spec: ResearchProtocol
Purpose:
  The standing protocol for ALL research rounds in SDDRA — the rules the
  RS1 arm and /sdd-research execute. Distilled from rounds 1-3 practice
  and 2026 deep-research landscape patterns (r2, round 3; all pipeline
  pattern sources cited in arms/research.sdd).

Owns: workflow/research-protocol.sdd

Lifecycle:
  STAGED -> IN_PROGRESS -> GATED (DECISIONS.md final) -> INTEGRATED -> DELETED
  (audit trail preserved in history.json + integrated artifacts carry citations)

RoundContract:
  Every research round produces, in tmp/research/{date}-{slug}/:
    SOURCES.md      — index + protocol reminder + internal baseline notes
    r{N}-{topic}.md — per-stream findings, every claim URL-cited
    DECISIONS.md    — per-finding INTEGRATE/SKIP + Pareto rationale + plan
  Integration writes ONLY to .sdd/ with provenance; then the folder is deleted.

VerificationGates:
  anchor_gate:      every claim has an inline source URL; unanchored prose
                    rejected (scholar-deep-research pattern)
  url_gate:         cited URLs existence-checked (3-13% DR citation
                    hallucination — arXiv 2604.03173)
  confidence_gate:  thin/contradictory claims marked LOW_CONFIDENCE, never
                    presented as established
  license_gate:     importable content MIT/Apache-2.0 ONLY; source-available
                    and unlicensed = blocked ([IMP6])
  pareto_gate:      integrate only >= 80% relevance; SKIP logged with reason

ParallelismRules:
  subagent_cap: 3-5 (Anthropic too-many-subagents failure documented)
  streams: 2-5 background research streams per round
  compressed_returns: streams return summaries + sources, never raw dumps
  single_threaded_writes: integration is done by ONE writer (D0 discipline)

BudgetRules:
  depth/breadth fixed at Scope approval; deterministic termination
  wall-clock cap per round (default 30 min)
  SKIP-heavy rounds are valid outcomes — the DECISIONS log is the evidence

FetchRules:
  DOM/accessibility-tree first (Playwright-class tooling); vision fallback
    only for JS-heavy/canvas pages (3-5x token economics)
  egress-gated fetches (LDR pattern) — fetched content is untrusted input
  Docker-gated execution for any code-bearing analysis [R59]-[R66]

HistoryIntegration:
  Every round appends an execution record to .claude/sdd/history.json:
    topic, streams, findings counts, integrated artifacts, staging deletion.
  Rounds are numbered in tmp-analysis.sdd logs for the sddra project.

Rules:
  [RP-01] No research round without a DECISIONS gate — findings never
          integrate directly from streams.
  [RP-02] No integration without provenance citations ([IMP1]).
  [RP-03] No staging survives integration — tmp ends empty ([RS1-08]).
  [RP-04] No benchmark/vendor number is decision-grade without independent
          reproduction (LoCoMo audit lesson — 6.4% wrong answer key).
  [RP-05] Background streams never write to .sdd/ — only the integrator.

